config DEMO_DEVICE
	bool "Virtual demo device driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_DEMO_DEVICE_ENABLED
	help
	  Enable the virtual demo device driver.

	  This driver has no real hardware — every call to demo_enable(),
	  demo_disable(), or demo_get_status() emits a log message and
	  updates internal state. It is designed to demonstrate how custom
	  Zephyr driver classes work.

	  The driver is enabled automatically when a DT node with
	  compatible = "demo-device" and status = "okay" is present.
